1. SCOPE & PURPOSE OF THIS REPOSITORY
-------------------------------------
This repository ("PRISM-118 · Periodic Console") is published strictly as a
publicly viewable Design Study & Interactive Prototype Archive to document
original visual design authorship and allow personal browser preview of the
design concept. This repository is NOT open-source software and grants no
open-source license (such as MIT, Apache, or GPL).

2. PERMITTED PERSONAL VIEWING & ATTRIBUTED REFERENCE
----------------------------------------------------
Subject to strict compliance with Section 3, RMvdesi grants visitors a limited,
revocable, non-exclusive, non-transferable, royalty-free personal permission to:

  (a) View, read, and inspect the design notes, renders, shaders, and prototype
      source code online for personal viewing and technical study;
  (b) Open and interact with the live design preview in a personal web browser
      (via GitHub Pages, local personal HTTP server, or offline file://); and
  (c) Capture and share unaltered screenshots, screen recordings, or brief
      illustrative excerpts for non-commercial editorial reviews, design
      critiques, or academic citation, PROVIDED THAT clear attribution is given
      to RMvdesi and this repository
      (https://github.com/RMvdesi/prism-periodic-console).

3. STRICT PROHIBITIONS (ALL RIGHTS RESERVED)
--------------------------------------------
Except as expressly permitted in Section 2 (and excluding the third-party open-
source font files listed in Section 5), NO license or right is granted — whether
express, implied, or by estoppel — under any copyright, trade dress, industrial
design, or other intellectual property right. Without prior written permission
from RMvdesi, you MAY NOT:

  (a) Copy, reproduce, republish, mirror, or redistribute the source code,
      GLSL shaders, baked dual-mode optical/mineral screen plates, PBR grain
      assets, acoustic synthesis graphs, concept studies, or renders in whole
      or in part;
  (b) Clone, port, adapt, translate, or incorporate the PRISM-118 console
      visual design, 118-element + AUX-06 triptych layout, dual-mode screen
      plates, sea-glass/ice-jade keycap shaders, or interaction mechanics into
      any third-party software, plugin, browser extension, theme pack, web
      application, or hardware/software product;
  (c) Use any original portion of this repository for commercial purposes, paid
      products, monetized services, or AI training/dataset ingestion; or
  (d) Remove, obscure, or alter any copyright header, license notice, or
      attribution metadata.

